WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT DO
  * IT DOES NOT WEAKEN THE REFUSAL. `_instrument_rows` and the refusal block
    in `_present` are not touched by any hunk, and the figure list is
    consulted AFTER the refusal returns, so a bundle with no recognisable
    control block still draws nothing -- the assumptions sheet included.
    Measured on both acts, below.
  * IT REINTRODUCES NO FABRICATED VALUE. Every new cell goes through `_fmt`,
    which takes no numeric default. Grepping the patched file for a numeric
    second argument to `dict.get` returns nothing. Where a value is genuinely
    absent the honest fallback string stands: `_display_spec` returns full
    precision rather than guessing, and `_columns_table` writes NOT_RECORDED
    into a column whose key a row does not carry rather than dropping the
    column or standing a number in for it.
  * It renames no bundle key and regenerates no figure. The bundle at
    docs/campaigns/T-family/demo/figures_actA/actA_screen_data.json is read
    exactly as it stands at HEAD.

RESTART SCOPE -- THIS ONE NEEDS A BOUNCE
  This is Python inside a module the control-room server imports, so IT DOES
  NOT TAKE EFFECT UNTIL THE SERVER RESTARTS. It should be batched into the
  single coordinated restart rather than bouncing a server Sanaa is sitting
  in. Bundle JSON and figure files are read inside `main()` at mission-run
  time (`_load_bundle` is called from the mission body, not at import), so
  producer-side work is data-only and lands on the next mission run with no
  bounce -- and after this patch, a bundle-supplied `extra_figures` or
  `result_table_columns` is data-only too.

